 # MedVital
-Astronaut health monitoring system built for NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (NYC). Simulated spacesuit/wearable sensors stream vitals in real time over a Cloudflare-secured network, flag anomalies, and send emergency alerts via Twilio.
 
-## Repository contents
+Astronaut health monitoring for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (New York City). A software-simulated wearable streams
+each astronaut's heart rate, blood oxygen and radiation dose to the spacecraft. The spacecraft runs on Cloudflare: it
+double-checks every reading, compares it with that astronaut's own pre-flight baseline, buzzes the wearable when
+something is wrong, and syncs everything to NASA over the link to Earth without losing a record when the link drops.
 
-* `nasa/` and `spacecraft-sync/`: Carl Wendy Simea's prototype code (see those folders).
-* `backend/`, `frontend/`, `docs/`, `tools/`: the MEDVITAL offline-first observation platform described below
-  (merged from branch `feat/backend-m3`).
+It focuses on four astronaut health risks: radiation, bone, heart and behavioral health (sleep and stress).
 
-## MEDVITAL observation platform
+## Run it
 
-Offline-first astronaut health observation platform — NASA Space Apps 2026 project.
+You need Python 3.11 or newer. From the repo root:
 
-MEDVITAL records health observations across four independent modules —
-**Radiation**, **Bone health**, **Cardiovascular health**, **Behavioral health** — and
-keeps every value labelled by origin: **simulated**, **measured** or **modeled**.
+```sh
+python start.py --fresh
+```
 
-> **Status: v0.1 foundation.** Schema, provenance, API contract, sync design, four module
-> skeletons with documented calculations, simulated astronaut profiles, and test
-> infrastructure. There is **no dashboard** and **no AI engine** yet.
+The first run creates `.venv/` and installs the backend (a few minutes, once). Then it starts the NASA receiver and the
+spacecraft hub and opens the apps in your browser:
 
-### Read this first
+| App | URL | Who it is |
+|---|---|---|
+| Astronaut 1 / Astronaut 2 | <http://localhost:8000/astronaut/?id=astro-1> | The wearable plus the astronaut's MedVital station. One tab per astronaut. |
+| Spacecraft hub | <http://localhost:8000/cloudflare/> | The Cloudflare side: live traffic through the private network, crew overview, database, verification. |
+| NASA | <http://localhost:5000/> | The flight surgeon's mission record. |
+| 3D body | <http://localhost:8000/body/?astronaut=astro-1> | The rotatable 3D body, fed live from the spacecraft. |
 
-* **No real data ships with this repository.** Every number in the running system today
-  is *simulated* test signal with arbitrary magnitudes. None is derived from NASA data.
-* MEDVITAL is **not a medical device**. It gives **no diagnosis**, **no medical advice**,
-  and applies **no clinical thresholds**.
-* NASA sources are catalogued in [docs/NASA_SOURCES.md](docs/NASA_SOURCES.md) as
-  *candidates, unverified*. Nothing has been ingested.
+`Ctrl+C` stops everything. Mission data stays in `runtime/`; `--fresh` starts a clean mission.
 
